rico's flu-related absence from the trail drew scrutiny just as early voting begins; a strong Paxton debate performance or polling shift toward the GOP could tighten this into a true tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: John Cornyn (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Texas's Senate seat is open for the first time in years after John Cornyn lost renomination to Ken Paxton, whose contested primary has left Republicans divided. Democrat James Talarico has outraised Paxton by a wide margin and holds a large cash advantage, while outside groups have spent heavily attacking Paxton. Polling since late September shows Talarico leading by roughly two to six points, with averages clustering around three points.\n\nExpert raters are split between Tossup and Lean D, and prediction markets price Talarico's chances in the low-to-mid 60s. The race remains competitive given Texas's Republican fundamentals, but the weight of polling, money, and market pricing points to a narrow Democratic edge heading into early voting.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6697, "margin": 2.08}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6924, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7255, "margin": 2.8}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6997, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6523, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6444, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6983, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7151, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.701, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7008, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6832, "margin": 2.2}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7125, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7022, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6597, "margin": 2.6}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6724, "margin": 2.8}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6815, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.6849, "marg